# Copy to gluetun/vpn.env (gitignored). Keep exactly one provider block.
# Switching providers: replace this file, then `docker compose up -d`.
# Nothing else changes: inside the namespace the tunnel is always tun0 and the
# downloader is always reached as http://gluetun:8001.
#
# No VPN account password is ever collected. Every path below uses a key or a
# config the provider issues for manual WireGuard setups, revocable from the
# provider's dashboard without touching the account.

# --- NordVPN (NordLynx is WireGuard; Nord issues a private key, not a file)
# Nord account site > NordVPN > Manual setup > access token, then:
#   curl -s -u token:TOKEN https://api.nordvpn.com/v1/users/services/credentials
# and copy nordlynx_private_key from the response.
VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=nordvpn
VPN_TYPE=wireguard
WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=
SERVER_COUNTRIES=Canada
# Optional narrowing: SERVER_CITIES, SERVER_CATEGORIES (see the gluetun wiki).

# --- Mullvad, Proton, AirVPN, IVPN or any provider that hands out a WireGuard
# .conf file: save it as gluetun/wg0.conf, start with the overlay
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f compose.wgfile.yml up -d
# and set only these two. gluetun reads every field from the file. The
# Endpoint line must be an IP address, not a hostname.
# VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=custom
# VPN_TYPE=wireguard

# --- Any provider gluetun supports natively (OpenVPN or WireGuard):
# https://github.com/qdm12/gluetun-wiki/tree/main/setup/providers
# VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=mullvad
# VPN_TYPE=wireguard
# WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=
# WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=
# SERVER_COUNTRIES=
